177. Identify the Two Quality Gates 

Question 

Identify the two important quality gates in the pipeline. 

Answer 

Quality Gate 1 — Schema Validation 

This occurs before loading the raw data into the staging table. 

Checks 

Required columns exist  

Column names are correct  

Data types are correct  

customerID exists  

CSV structure matches the expected schema  

If validation fails 

Invalid data 

   ↓ 

Stop Pipeline 

   ↓ 

Log Error 

   ↓ 

Do not load into staging 

 

Quality Gate 2 — Data Quality Check 

This occurs before building the feature table. 

Checks 

No duplicate customer_id  

Required columns are not NULL  

tenure >= 0  

monthly_charges >= 0  

Valid contract types  

Valid payment methods  

Valid churn values  

Numeric values are valid  

If validation fails 

Bad Data 

   ↓ 

Stop Feature Generation 

   ↓ 

Log / Quarantine Error 

 

178. Define the Incremental Processing Strategy 

Question 

What should happen when the same customer appears in two consecutive daily extracts? 

Answer 

Use customer_id as the natural key and implement an upsert strategy. 

Customer ID exists? 

      │ 

  ┌───┴───┐ 

  │       │ 

 Yes      No 

  │       │ 

UPDATE   INSERT 

Example 

If customer 7590-VHVEG already exists and appears again in today's extract, the existing record should be updated instead of creating a duplicate. 

This makes the pipeline idempotent. 

Running the same input multiple times should produce the same final database state. 

 

